Per-file headers
----------------

The imported subtree carried no SPDX headers upstream. 271 real source files
(235 `.py`, 36 `.rs`) were tagged on import with
`SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-or-later` and a pointer to this file.

The 387 files under `vendor/browseros/chromium_patches/` were deliberately NOT
tagged. They are unified diffs against a Chromium checkout -- two of them are
even named `.py` -- and prepending a header line would stop them applying. They
are covered by this NOTICE and by `LICENSE`.

Binary assets, images, markdown and build configuration carry no header either,
which is how upstream ships them.


Chromium base
-------------

The imported patch set is cut against Chromium `155.0.8059.26`
(`16c3e55476d3564bea713314b2fff638749ce3e6`), recorded upstream in
`vendor/browseros/BASE_COMMIT`. This repository's own patch set in `patches/`
is cut against `153.0.8010.36`; reconciling the two is tracked work, not a
property of this import.


What was NOT imported
---------------------

Upstream has exactly two packages: `packages/browseros` (imported here) and
`packages/browseros-agent`. It tracks **no** Chromium checkout -- the build
system downloads one, so there was never a 100 GB directory to leave behind.

- `packages/browseros-agent` -- the agent apps, server, TypeScript packages and
  Rust crates. Imported separately into `redrob-labs/redrob-browser-agent`.
- `.internal-docs` -- a private upstream submodule (`git@`), not accessible.
- Two `__pycache__/*.pyc` files that upstream tracks by accident. They are
  generated CPython bytecode, regenerated on first run, and are dropped from
  this tree rather than carried. The history that created them is still present.
